msgstr "git-push(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:7
#, placeholders:'git-push', priority:220
msgid "git-push - Update remote refs along with associated objects"
msgstr "git-push - Atualiza as refs remotas junto com os objetos associados a ela"

#. type: synopsis
#: en/git-push.adoc:18
#, ignore-ellipsis, no-wrap, placeholders:'[--all':'--branches':'--mirror':'--tags]':'[--follow-tags]':'[--atomic]':'--dry-run]':'[--receive-pack=':'git-receive-pack':'[--repo=':'--force]':'--delete]':'[--prune]':'--quiet]':'--verbose]':'--set-upstream]':'--push-option=':'--signed=(true|false|if-asked)]':'[--force-with-lease':'[--force-if-includes]':'[--no-verify]', priority:220
msgid ""
"git push [--all | --branches | --mirror | --tags] [--follow-tags] [--atomic] [-n | --dry-run] [--receive-pack=<git-receive-pack>]\n"
"\t [--repo=<repository>] [-f | --force] [-d | --delete] [--prune] [-q | --quiet] [-v | --verbose]\n"
"\t [-u | --set-upstream] [-o <string> | --push-option=<string>]\n"
"\t [--[no-]signed | --signed=(true|false|if-asked)]\n"
"\t [--force-with-lease[=<refname>[:<expect>]] [--force-if-includes]]\n"
"\t [--no-verify] [<repository> [<refspec>...]]\n"
msgstr ""
"git push [--all | --branches | --mirror | --tags] [--follow-tags] [--atomic] [-n | --dry-run] [--receive-pack=<git-receive-pack>]\n"
"\t[--repo=<repositório>] [-f | --force] [-d | --delete] [--prune] [-q | --quiet] [-v | --verbose]\n"
"\t[-u | --set-upstream] [-o <texto> | --push-option=<texto>]\n"
"\t[--[no-]signed | --signed=(true|false|if-asked)]\n"
"\t[--force-with-lease[=<refname>[:<expect>]] [--force-if-includes]]\n"
"\t[--no-verify] [<repositório> [<refspec>...]]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:24
#, priority:220
msgid "Updates one or more branches, tags, or other references in one or more remote repositories from your local repository, and sends all necessary data that isn't already on the remote."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:28
#, priority:220
msgid "The simplest way to push is `git push <remote> <branch>`. `git push origin main` will push the local `main` branch to the `main` branch on the remote named `origin`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:32
#, priority:220
msgid "You can also push to multiple remotes at once by using a remote group. A remote group is a named list of remotes configured via `remotes.<name>` in your git config:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:34
#, no-wrap, placeholders:'remotes.all', priority:220
msgid "\t$ git config remotes.all-remotes \"origin gitlab backup\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:40
#, placeholders:'linkgit:git-config[1]', priority:220
msgid "Then `git push all-remotes` will push to `origin`, `gitlab`, and `backup` in turn, as if you had run `git push` against each one individually. Each remote is pushed independently using its own push mapping configuration. There is a `remotes.<group>` entry in the configuration file. (See linkgit:git-config[1])."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:43
#, priority:220
msgid "The `<repository>` argument defaults to the upstream for the current branch, or `origin` if there's no configured upstream."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:46
#, priority:220
msgid "To decide which branches, tags, or other refs to push, Git uses (in order of precedence):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:49
#, placeholders:'`--all`':'`--mirror`':'`--tags`', priority:220
msgid "The `<refspec>` argument(s) (for example `main` in `git push origin main`) or the `--all`, `--mirror`, or `--tags` options"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:50
#, priority:220
msgid "The `remote.<name>.push` configuration for the repository being pushed to"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:53
#, placeholders:'push.default':'push.default':'<<CONFIGURATION,':'push.default', priority:220
msgid "The `push.default` configuration. The default is `push.default=simple`, which will push to a branch with the same name as the current branch. See the <<CONFIGURATION,CONFIGURATION>> section below for more on `push.default`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:58
#, placeholders:'push.default', priority:220
msgid "`git push` may fail if you haven't set an upstream for the current branch, depending on what `push.default` is set to. See the <<UPSTREAM-BRANCHES,UPSTREAM BRANCHES>> section below for more on how to set and use upstreams."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:62
#, placeholders:'linkgit:git-receive-pack[1]', priority:220
msgid "You can make interesting things happen to a repository every time you push into it, by setting up 'hooks' there. See documentation for linkgit:git-receive-pack[1]."
msgstr "É possível fazer com que coisas interessantes aconteçam num repositório toda vez que você fizer um \"push\" nele, ao configurar \"ganchos\" nele. Consulte a documentação para linkgit:git-receive-pack[1]."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/git-push.adoc:66 en/pull-fetch-param.adoc:1 en/git-clone.adoc:362 en/git-pull.adoc:46
#, fuzzy, no-wrap, priority:300
#| msgid "<repository>"
msgid "_<repository>_"
msgstr "<repositório>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:73
#, fuzzy, placeholders:'<<URLS,':'<<REMOTES,', priority:220
#| msgid "The \"remote\" repository that is the destination of a push operation. This parameter can be either a URL (see the section <<URLS,GIT URLS>> below) or the name of a remote (see the section <<REMOTES,REMOTES>> below)."
msgid "The \"remote\" repository that is the destination of a push operation. This parameter can be either a URL (see the section <<URLS,GIT URLS>> below), the name of a remote (see the section <<REMOTES,REMOTES>> below), or the name of a remote group (see the section <<REMOTE-GROUPS,REMOTE GROUPS>> below)."
msgstr "O repositório \"remote\" que é o destino de uma operação 'push'. Este parâmetro pode ser uma URL (consulte a seção <<URLS,GIT URLS>> abaixo) ou o nome de um controle remoto (consulte a seção <<REMOTES,RAMOS REMOTOS>> abaixo)."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/git-push.adoc:74
#, fuzzy, ignore-ellipsis, no-wrap, priority:220
#| msgid "<refspec>..."
msgid "`<refspec>...`"
msgstr "<refspec>..."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:76
#, priority:220
msgid "Specify what destination ref to update with what source object."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:79
#, priority:220
msgid "The format for a refspec is `[+]<src>[:<dst>]`, for example `main`, `main:other`, or `HEAD^:refs/heads/main`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:82
#, fuzzy, placeholders:'linkgit:gitrevisions[7]', priority:220
#| msgid "The <src> is often the name of the branch you would want to push, but it can be any arbitrary \"SHA-1 expression\", such as `master~4` or `HEAD` (see linkgit:gitrevisions[7])."
msgid "The _<src>_ is often the name of the local branch to push, but it can be any arbitrary \"SHA-1 expression\" (see linkgit:gitrevisions[7])."
msgstr "Geralmente `<src>` é o nome do ramo que você deseja impulsionar, pode ser qualquer \"expressão SHA-1\" arbitrária, como `master~4` ou `HEAD` (consulte linkgit:gitrevisions[7])."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:85
#, priority:220
msgid "The _<dst>_ determines what ref to update on the remote side. It must be the name of a branch, tag, or other ref, not an arbitrary expression."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:87
#, placeholders:'`--force`', priority:220
msgid "The `+` is optional and does the same thing as `--force`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:93
#, priority:220
msgid "You can write a refspec using the fully expanded form (for example `refs/heads/main:refs/heads/main`) which specifies the exact source and destination, or with a shorter form (for example `main` or `main:other`). Here are the rules for how refspecs are expanded, as well as various other special refspec forms:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:98
#, fuzzy, priority:220
#| msgid "If <src> resolves to a ref starting with refs/heads/ or refs/tags/, then prepend that to <dst>."
msgid "_<src>_ without a `:<dst>` means to update the same ref as the _<src>_, unless the `remote.<repository>.push` configuration specifies a different _<dst>_. For example, if `main` is a branch, then the refspec `main` expands to `main:refs/heads/main`."
msgstr "Caso o <src> seja resolvido para uma \"ref\" começando com `refs/heads/` ou `refs/tags/`, coloque um prefixo no <dst>."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:101
#, fuzzy, priority:220
#| msgid "If <dst> unambiguously refers to a ref on the <repository> remote, then push to that ref."
msgid "If _<dst>_ unambiguously refers to a ref on the <repository> remote, then expand it to that ref. For example, if `v1.0` is a tag on the remote, then `HEAD:v1.0` expands to `HEAD:refs/tags/v1.0`."
msgstr "Caso o <dst> se refira inequivocamente a uma \"ref\" no <repositório> do ramo remoto, então faça um impulsionamento \"push\" nesta ref."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:104
#, fuzzy, priority:220
#| msgid "If <src> resolves to a ref starting with refs/heads/ or refs/tags/, then prepend that to <dst>."
msgid "If _<src>_ resolves to a ref starting with `refs/heads/` or `refs/tags/`, then prepend that to <dst>. For example, if `main` is a branch, then `main:other` expands to `main:refs/heads/other`"
msgstr "Caso o <src> seja resolvido para uma \"ref\" começando com `refs/heads/` ou `refs/tags/`, coloque um prefixo no <dst>."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:108
#, priority:220
msgid "The special refspec `:` (or `+:` to allow non-fast-forward updates) directs Git to push \"matching\" branches: for every branch that exists on the local side, the remote side is updated if a branch of the same name already exists on the remote side."
msgstr "O refspec especial `:` (ou `+:` para permitir atualizações que não sejam de avanço rápido) direciona o Git a enviar ramificações \"correspondentes\": para cada ramificação que existe no lado local, o lado remoto é atualizado quando uma ramificação com o mesmo nome já existir no lado remoto."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:114
#, fuzzy, priority:220
#| msgid "A <refspec> may contain a `*` in its <src> to indicate a simple pattern match. Such a refspec functions like a glob that matches any ref with the same prefix. A pattern <refspec> must have a `*` in both the <src> and <dst>. It will map refs to the destination by replacing the `*` with the contents matched from the source."
msgid "_<src>_ may contain a `*` to indicate a simple pattern match. This works like a glob that matches any ref matching the pattern. There must be only one `*` in both the `<src>` and `<dst>`. It will map refs to the destination by replacing the * with the contents matched from the source. For example, `refs/heads/*:refs/heads/*` will push all branches."
msgstr "Uma <refspec> pode conter um `*` na sua origem <src> para indicar uma simples combinação de padrões. Tal \"refspec\" funciona como um \"glob\" que combina com qualquer ref de mesmo prefixo. Um padrão <refspec> deve conter um `*` tanto origem <src> quanto no destino <dst>. Ele irá mapear os reffs para o destino substituindo o `*` pelo conteúdo correspondente da fonte."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:122
#, priority:220
msgid "A refspec starting with `^` is a negative refspec. This specifies refs to exclude. A ref will be considered to match if it matches at least one positive refspec, and does not match any negative refspec. Negative refspecs can be pattern refspecs. They must only contain a _<src>_. Fully spelled out hex object names are also not supported. For example, `git push origin 'refs/heads/*' '^refs/heads/dev-*'` will push all branches except for those starting with `dev-`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:125
#, priority:220
msgid "If _<src>_ is empty, it deletes the _<dst>_ ref from the remote repository. For example, `git push origin :dev` will delete the `dev` branch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:126
#, fuzzy, priority:220
#| msgid "`tag <tag>` means the same as `refs/tags/<tag>:refs/tags/<tag>`."
msgid "`tag <tag>` expands to `refs/tags/<tag>:refs/tags/<tag>`."
msgstr "A `tag <tag>` significa o mesmo que `refs/tags/<tag>:refs/tags/<tag>`."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:129
#, priority:220
msgid "This is technically a special syntax for `git push` and not a refspec, since in `git push origin tag v1.0` the arguments `tag` and `v1.0` are separate."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:134
#, fuzzy, placeholders:'advice.pushUnqualifiedRefname':'linkgit:git-config[1]', priority:220
#| msgid "Other ambiguity resolutions might be added in the future, but for now any other cases will error out with an error indicating what we tried, and depending on the `advice.pushUnqualifiedRefname` configuration (see linkgit:git-config[1]) suggest what refs/ namespace you may have wanted to push to."
msgid "If the refspec can't be expanded unambiguously, error out with an error indicating what was tried, and depending on the `advice.pushUnqualifiedRefname` configuration (see linkgit:git-config[1]) suggest what refs/ namespace you may have wanted to push to."
msgstr "Outras resoluções de ambiguidade podem ser adicionadas no futuro, mas, por enquanto, outros casos apresentarão um erro indicando o que tentamos e dependendo da configuração `advice.pushUnqualifiedRefname` (consulte linkgit:git-config[1]), sugere qual 'refs/ namespace' você possa querer impulsionar."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:136
#, priority:220
msgid "Not all updates are allowed: see PUSH RULES below for the details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/git-push.adoc:137 en/git-reflog.adoc:91 en/git-reflog.adoc:103 en/git-branch.adoc:191 en/git-commit.adoc:68 en/git-stash.adoc:169 en/rev-list-options.adoc:167 en/git-add.adoc:134 en/git-describe.adoc:50 en/git-submodule.adoc:297 en/fetch-options.adoc:1
#, ignore-same, no-wrap, priority:300
msgid "`--all`"
msgstr "`--all`"

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/git-push.adoc:138
#, ignore-same, no-wrap, priority:220
msgid "`--branches`"
msgstr "`--branches`"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:141
#, priority:220
msgid "Push all branches (i.e. refs under `refs/heads/`); cannot be used with other <refspec>."
msgstr "impulsione todos os ramos (ou seja, refs em `refs/heads/`); não pode ser utilizado com outro <refspec>."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/git-push.adoc:142 en/fetch-options.adoc:190
#, ignore-same, no-wrap, priority:220
msgid "`--prune`"
msgstr "`--prune`"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:149
#, placeholders:'--prune', priority:220
msgid "Remove remote branches that don't have a local counterpart. For example a remote branch `tmp` will be removed if a local branch with the same name doesn't exist any more. This also respects refspecs, e.g. `git push --prune remote refs/heads/*:refs/tmp/*` would make sure that remote `refs/tmp/foo` will be removed if `refs/heads/foo` doesn't exist."
msgstr "Remova as ramificações remotas que não têm uma contraparte local. Por exemplo, uma ramificação remota `tmp` será removida se uma ramificação local com o mesmo nome não existir mais. Isso também respeita os refspecs, por exemplo, o comando `git push --prune remote refs/heads/*:refs/tmp/*` garantiria que o remote `refs/tmp/foo` seria removido se `refs/heads/foo` não existisse."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/git-push.adoc:150 en/git-clone.adoc:218
#, ignore-same, no-wrap, priority:300
msgid "`--mirror`"
msgstr "`--mirror`"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:160
#, priority:220
msgid "Instead of naming each ref to push, specifies that all refs under `refs/` (which includes but is not limited to `refs/heads/`, `refs/remotes/`, and `refs/tags/`) be mirrored to the remote repository. Newly created local refs will be pushed to the remote end, locally updated refs will be force updated on the remote end, and deleted refs will be removed from the remote end. This is the default if the configuration option `remote.<remote>.mirror` is set."
msgstr "Em vez de nomear cada referência que será enviada, especifica que todas as refs em `refs/` (que inclui, mas não se limita a `refs/heads/`, `refs/remotes/` e `refs/tags/`) sejam espelhadas no repositório remoto. As refs locais recém-criadas serão enviadas para a extremidade remota, as refs atualizadas localmente serão atualizadas à força na extremidade remota e as refs excluídas serão removidas da extremidade remota. Esse é o padrão se a opção de configuração `remote.<remoto>.mirror` estiver definida."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/git-push.adoc:161 en/git-reflog.adoc:150 en/git-notes.adoc:217 en/git-commit.adoc:218 en/git-clone.adoc:160 en/git-shortlog.adoc:29 en/git-rm.adoc:52 en/merge-options.adoc:108 en/git-mv.adoc:38 en/git-add.adoc:67 en/git-worktree.adoc:250 en/fetch-options.adoc:218
#, ignore-same, no-wrap, priority:300
msgid "`-n`"
msgstr "`-n`"

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/git-push.adoc:162 en/git-reflog.adoc:151 en/git-notes.adoc:218 en/git-branch.adoc:238 en/git-commit.adoc:378 en/git-rm.adoc:53 en/git-mv.adoc:39 en/git-add.adoc:68 en/git-worktree.adoc:251 en/fetch-options.adoc:108
#, ignore-same, no-wrap, priority:300
msgid "`--dry-run`"
msgstr "`--dry-run`"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:164 en/git-send-pack.adoc:54 en/git-http-push.adoc:39
#, priority:220
msgid "Do everything except actually send the updates."
msgstr "Faça tudo, exceto realmente enviar as atualizações."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/git-push.adoc:165 en/git-commit.adoc:152 en/git-worktree.adoc:259 en/fetch-options.adoc:111
#, ignore-same, no-wrap, priority:280
msgid "`--porcelain`"
msgstr "`--porcelain`"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:169
#, priority:220
msgid "Produce machine-readable output. The output status line for each ref will be tab-separated and sent to stdout instead of stderr. The full symbolic names of the refs will be given."
msgstr "Produz resultados legíveis para máquina. A linha de status de saída para cada ref será separada por tabulação e enviada para stdout em vez de stderr. Os nomes simbólicos completos dos refs serão fornecidos."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/git-push.adoc:170 en/git-branch.adoc:101 en/git-tag.adoc:91 en/git-switch.adoc:84 en/git-worktree.adoc:204 en/git-checkout.adoc:208
#, ignore-same, no-wrap, priority:260
msgid "`-d`"
msgstr "`-d`"

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/git-push.adoc:171 en/git-branch.adoc:102 en/git-tag.adoc:92
#, ignore-same, no-wrap, priority:260
msgid "`--delete`"
msgstr "`--delete`"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:174
#, priority:220
msgid "All listed refs are deleted from the remote repository. This is the same as prefixing all refs with a colon."
msgstr "Todas as refs listadas são excluídas do repositório remoto. É o mesmo que prefixar todos as refs com dois pontos."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/git-push.adoc:175 en/git-clone.adoc:301 en/git-describe.adoc:55 en/fetch-options.adoc:249
#, ignore-same, no-wrap, priority:300
msgid "`--tags`"
msgstr "`--tags`"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:179
#, priority:220
msgid "All refs under `refs/tags` are pushed, in addition to refspecs explicitly listed on the command line."
msgstr "Todas as refs no `refs/tags` são impulsionadas, além das \"refspecs\" que forem explicitamente listados na linha de comando."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/git-push.adoc:180
#, ignore-same, no-wrap, priority:220
msgid "`--follow-tags`"
msgstr "`--follow-tags`"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-push.adoc:187
#, placeholders:'push.followTags':'push.followTags':'linkgit:git-config[1]', priority:220
msgid "Push all the refs that would be pushed without this option, and also push annotated tags in `refs/tags` that are missing from the remote but are pointing at commit-ish that are reachable from the refs being pushed. This can also be specified with configuration variable `push.followTags`. For more information, see `push.followTags` in linkgit:git-config[1]."
msgstr "Envie todas as refs que seriam enviadas sem essa opção e também envie as etiquetas anotadas em `refs/tags` que estão faltando no controle remoto, mas que estão apontando para os commits que são acessíveis a partir das refs que estão sendo enviadas. Isso também pode ser definido na variável de configuração `push.followTags`. Para mais informações consulte `push.followTags` do comando linkgit:git-config[1]."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/git-push.adoc:188 en/git-push.adoc:198
#, ignore-same, no-wrap, priority:220
msgid "`--signed`"
msgstr "`--signed`"

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/git-push.adoc:189 en/git-push.adoc:195
#, ignore-same, no-wrap, priority:220
msgid "`--no-signed`"
