msgstr "git-check-mailmap(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-check-mailmap.adoc:7
#, placeholders:'git-check-mailmap', priority:10
msgid "git-check-mailmap - Show canonical names and email addresses of contacts"
msgstr "git-check-mailmap - Exiba os nomes canônicos e os endereços de e-mail dos contatos"

#. type: verse
#: en/git-check-mailmap.adoc:13
#, ignore-ellipsis, no-wrap, placeholders:'git check-mailmap', priority:10
msgid "'git check-mailmap' [<options>] <contact>...\n"
msgstr "'git check-mailmap' [<opções>] <contato>...\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-check-mailmap.adoc:22
#, fuzzy, placeholders:'$user':'`--stdin`', priority:10
#| msgid "For each ``Name $$<user@host>$$'' or ``$$<user@host>$$'' from the command-line or standard input (when using `--stdin`), look up the person's canonical name and email address (see \"Mapping Authors\" below). If found, print them; otherwise print the input as-is."
msgid "For each ``Name $$<user@host>$$'', ``$$<user@host>$$'', or ``$$user@host$$'' from the command-line or standard input (when using `--stdin`), look up the person's canonical name and email address (see \"Mapping Authors\" below). If found, print them; otherwise print the input as-is."
msgstr "Para cada ``Name $$<user@host>$$'' ou ``$$<user@host>$$'' na linha de comando ou na entrada padrão (ao utilizar o `--stdin`), procure o nome canônico e o endereço do e-mail da pessoa (consulte \"Mapeando os autores\" logo abaixo). Se encontrado, exiba-os; caso contrário, exiba a entrada como estiver."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-check-mailmap.adoc:29
#, priority:10
msgid "Read contacts, one per line, from the standard input after exhausting contacts provided on the command-line."
msgstr "Leia os contatos, um por linha, a partir da entrada padrão após esgotar os contatos informados na linha de comando."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/git-check-mailmap.adoc:30
#, fuzzy, no-wrap, placeholders:'--mailmap-file=', priority:10
#| msgid "--add-file=<file>"
msgid "--mailmap-file=<file>"
msgstr "--add-file=<arquivo>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-check-mailmap.adoc:34
#, priority:10
msgid "In addition to any configured mailmap files, read the specified mailmap file. Entries in this file take precedence over entries in either the default mailmap file or any configured mailmap file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/git-check-mailmap.adoc:35
#, fuzzy, no-wrap, placeholders:'--mailmap-blob=', priority:10
#| msgid "--blob <blob>"
msgid "--mailmap-blob=<blob>"
msgstr "--blob <bolha>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-check-mailmap.adoc:40
#, placeholders:'`--mailmap-file`':'`--mailmap-file`':'`--mailmap-blob`':'`--mailmap-file`', priority:10
msgid "Like `--mailmap-file`, but consider the value as a reference to a blob in the repository. If both `--mailmap-file` and `--mailmap-blob` are specified, entries in `--mailmap-file` will take precedence."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-check-mailmap.adoc:47
#, priority:10
msgid "For each contact, a single line is output, terminated by a newline. If the name is provided or known to the 'mailmap', ``Name $$<user@host>$$'' is printed; otherwise only ``$$<user@host>$$'' is printed."
msgstr "Para cada contato, é emitida uma única linha, terminada por uma nova linha. Se o nome for informado ou conhecido pelo 'mailmap', o ``Name $$<user@host>$$$'' será impresso; caso contrário, será impresso apenas ``$$<user@host>$$$''."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/git-check-mailmap.adoc:54
#, placeholders:'mailmap.file':'mailmap.blob':'linkgit:git-config[1]', priority:10
msgid "See `mailmap.file` and `mailmap.blob` in linkgit:git-config[1] for how to specify a custom `.mailmap` target file or object."
msgstr "Consulte `mailmap.file` e `mailmap.blob` no linkgit:git-config[1] para saber como definir um arquivo alvo `.mailmap` personalizado ou um objeto."

